{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nRecent GitHub Actions runs have remained stuck until another session manually cleared them. Use the repository `rebar-debug` protocol to prove the recurring mechanism and repair every confirmed defect in scope. Do not mutate live GitHub run state during investigation.\n\n## Plan\n### Phase 1 — Understand\n- Gather a descriptive dossier from authenticated Actions run/job metadata, timestamps, cancellation history, workflow definitions, repository settings, ticket/history evidence, and recent relevant changes.\n- Treat this as a chronic incident unless evidence disproves recurrence; generate falsifiable competing hypotheses through the skill-required independent investigation step.\n- Run read-only discriminating experiments and require runtime/API evidence of the mechanism before declaring a root cause. Establish defect legitimacy against repository workflow contracts or prior fixed behavior, then sweep callers/dependencies of the artifact proposed for change.\n\n### Phase 2 — Repair (only after Phase 1 proves a defect)\n- Read the skill test-design standard, inventory coverage, and create the smallest regression oracle that exercises the proven mechanism. Observe it RED for the expected reason before editing production workflow/code.\n- Implement the mechanism-level fix while the RED oracle is held out from the fixer, then restore it and prove GREEN. Seed the exact defect as a mutation and confirm the oracle returns RED before restoring the fix.\n- Run relevant workflow validation, lint/tests, and replicate the original stuck-run scenario through a local or read-only-safe equivalent. Sweep for confirmed siblings of the same pattern.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The affected run pattern is identified with URLs and timestamps, checked via `gh run list` and Actions API metadata.\n- [ ] A parsimonious root cause is confirmed by discriminating evidence that explains why manual clearing unsticks the queue and rejects competing runner-capacity, concurrency, workflow, and platform hypotheses.\n- [ ] Defect legitimacy and the bounded caller/dependency sweep are documented before any production edit.\n- [ ] Each confirmed defect has a regression oracle observed RED before the fix, GREEN after it, and RED again under a defect-seeded mutation.\n- [ ] Relevant `make lint`, targeted tests, Actions workflow validation, and a safe replication of the original scenario pass after the fix.\n- [ ] Findings, experiments, decisions, and final verification are recorded in `rebar comment` updates on this ticket.\n\n## Verification\nUse read-only `gh run list`, `gh run view`, and `gh api` queries; inspect `.github/workflows/` and relevant history; then run the exact targeted tests introduced for the confirmed mechanism plus `make lint` and the repository workflow validators. No live run cancellation, rerun, dispatch, or repository-setting change is authorized."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785543858607479001,"uuid":"fa7e6c5c-40de-4f1c-b8ff-332359fa0869"}